{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And HaShem showed him a tree and he cast it into the waters.</b> Even though it was in the power of HaShem to sweeten without a tree, it is His way to perform miracles according to the custom of the world, that one casts something sweet into something bitter. <b>Into the waters</b> — in the waters; <i>el</i> in place of the bet." "<b>There He made for him a statute and an ordinance.</b> As it is written after it: 'If you will surely listen,' etc. <b>A statute and an ordinance</b> — Rashi explained: the red heifer and civil laws. However, it was not made until the second year."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:05.252587960Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}